    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but isn't there a more objective way to look at it? i mean, if you look at the actual maps and the history of broken promises, doesn't it seem like the \"defensive\" argument is just a way to mask a clear attempt to weaken a rival power? it seems pretty obvious that the intent is containment, not just defense.",
